{{also|FELIX|Felix|Félix}}
==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-lw-i}}. Cognate with Ancient Greek {{m|grc|θῆλυς}}.<ref>{{R:De Vaan 2008}}</ref> See also {{l|la|fēmina}}, {{l|la|fētus}}, {{l|la|fēcundus}}, {{l|la|fēnus}}, {{l|la|fīlius}}, {{l|la|fellō}}. Other authors connect this and the previous with {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*bʰew-||to grow, produce}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈfeː.liːks/|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{la-adj-3rd-1E|fēlīx|fēlīcis}}

# [[happy]], [[lucky]], [[blessed]], [[fortunate]]
# [[fertile]], [[fruitful]]
# [[auspicious]], [[favorable]], of [[good]] [[omen]] or [[luck]]
# {{label|la|religion|archaic}} of the [[noble]] [[fruit]]s offered to the [[deity|deities]]

